Subject: Add ExternalApplication to the Fabrication user interface.
Summary: 
Shows how a basic ExternalApplication can be added to the Fabrication user interface. It uses a MessageBox to communicate information to the interactive user.

Classes: 
Autodesk.Fabrication.ApplicationServices.Application
Autodesk.Fabrication.Job

Project Files: 
·	Command.cs
This file contains a class named “Command” which inherits from the IExternalApplication interface. The function of the class is to add an external application to Autodesk Fabrication and create a Message Box in the Execute method to show some information to the user. The user can do anything in Execute method like reading Items and Database entries.

Description: 
The sample defines a class which inherits from IExternalApplication interface, and implements the Execute method, creating a message box in it’s body.

